{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790710508,"nonce":"BizNG9B4OzPKekg+AV4zB01+UWI=","message":"Performance follow-up implemented in Zyntax 985b990a and Caribou bc0af16.\n\nTyped host schemas now carry opaque keyed call sites, so Float getters, setters and methods avoid repeated name interning, lookup and scalar boxing. Function return shapes survive both Ash runtime publication and Python inference; a returned `Fn(Float) -\u003e Float` therefore uses the fixed scalar ABI instead of the dynamic foreign call. Zyntax exports publish the stable atomic call cell, and the bridge loads its current entry for every call, including warmed direct call sites. A regression test swaps that cell after warming a site and proves the next call reaches the replacement entry.\n\nNative matrix, 1,000,000 iterations, median of seven runs, hybrid Ash and tiered WrenLift:\n\n| operation | Haxe-\u003eWren | Wren-\u003eHaxe | Python-\u003eHaxe | Python-\u003eWren |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| static | 39.6 ns | 25.8 ns | 32.2 ns | 33.0 ns |\n| method | 50.2 ns | 35.7 ns | 53.8 ns | 49.0 ns |\n| getter | 45.4 ns | 21.0 ns | 17.0 ns | 33.3 ns |\n| setter | 50.1 ns | 19.9 ns | 18.6 ns | 34.1 ns |\n| closure | 55.1 ns | 45.2 ns | 48.9 ns | 65.9 ns |\n| construct | 125.3 ns | 102.2 ns | 170.8 ns | 277.8 ns |\n\nScalar and closure crossings are now in the range of the established Haxe/Wren bridge. Construction remains dominated by allocating and crossing a new managed object on every iteration.\n\nPassing checks: Zyntax foreign-object integration (including a typed host closure), Caribou Python/Python-Haxe/Python-foreign integration, and the atomic current-entry bridge regression.\n\nThe issue remains open for Python-owned objects and closures crossing outward, future awaiting, and the Lua follow-ups already listed above.","files":null}]}